---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Kadanco"
  description="Privacy policy for kadanco.com, operated by Kadanco UG (haftungsbeschränkt), Berlin."
>
  <main>
    <!-- branded header band so the nav sits on dark, then switches over the light body -->
    <section class="legal-hero band-deep" data-theme="dark">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="updated">Last updated: June 2026</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-body" data-theme="light">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="legal">

          <h3>Controller</h3>
          <p>
            The controller responsible for data processing on this website is Kadanco UG
            (haftungsbeschr&auml;nkt), Prenzlauer Allee 186, 10405 Berlin, Germany. Email:
            <a href="mailto:hello@kadanco.com">hello@kadanco.com</a>.
          </p>

          <h3>What is personal data?</h3>
          <p>
            Personal data is any information relating to an identified or identifiable natural person
            (Art. 4 GDPR), for example your name, address, email address or telephone number.
          </p>

          <h3>Scope of data collection</h3>
          <p>
            Except as described below, no personal data is collected when you simply browse this website.
            Your browser transmits certain technical information so that the site can be delivered and
            kept secure.
          </p>

          <h3>Server log files</h3>
          <p>
            When you access this website, our hosting provider automatically collects and stores
            information that your browser transmits in server log files. This includes browser type and
            version, operating system, the referrer URL, the requesting page, and the date and time of
            the request. This data is not merged with other sources and is processed on the basis of our
            legitimate interest in the secure and stable operation of the website (Art. 6 (1)(f) GDPR).
          </p>

          <h3>Hosting</h3>
          <p>
            This website is hosted on Cloudflare Pages, provided by Cloudflare, Inc. As our processor,
            Cloudflare processes the server data described above on our behalf.
          </p>

          <h3>Contact form</h3>
          <p>
            You can contact us using the contact form on this website. The data you enter (your name,
            work email and the details you choose to provide) is transmitted to us so that we can handle
            your enquiry. Delivery of the form is handled by our processor Plunk. The legal basis is
            Art. 6 (1)(b) GDPR where your enquiry relates to a pre-contractual or contractual matter, and
            Art. 6 (1)(f) GDPR (our legitimate interest in responding) otherwise. We delete this data
            once your enquiry has been fully dealt with, unless statutory retention obligations apply.
          </p>

          <h3>Cookies</h3>
          <p>
            This website uses cookies. Strictly necessary cookies are always active so the site can
            function and stay secure. Analytics cookies are set only after you give your consent through
            our cookie banner, and you can change or withdraw that choice at any time (see "Cookie
            consent" below).
          </p>

          <h3>Analytics</h3>
          <p>
            We use Google Analytics 4 together with Google Tag Manager, services provided by Google
            Ireland Limited (Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland), to understand how this
            website is used. Analytics runs only after you give consent via our cookie banner. Until
            then, Google Consent Mode keeps it in a state that does not store information on or read it
            from your device. Where analytics is active, it may process usage data and your shortened IP
            address. The legal basis is your consent under Art. 6 (1)(a) GDPR, which you can withdraw at
            any time with effect for the future via the cookie settings. Data may be transferred to
            Google LLC in the USA. Google LLC is certified under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework, and
            standard contractual clauses apply as an additional safeguard. Further information is in
            Google's privacy policy at
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.
          </p>

          <h3>Cookie consent</h3>
          <p>
            Non-essential cookies, including analytics, are set only after you consent through our
            cookie banner, which is provided by CookieYes. You can change or withdraw your choice at any
            time using the cookie settings option offered by the banner. Withdrawing consent does not
            affect the lawfulness of any processing carried out before the withdrawal.
          </p>

          <h3>Your rights</h3>
          <p>
            Under the GDPR you have the right to access (Art. 15), rectification (Art. 16), erasure
            (Art. 17), restriction of processing (Art. 18), data portability (Art. 20), and to object to
            processing (Art. 21). Where processing is based on consent, you may withdraw that consent at
            any time with effect for the future. To exercise any of these rights, contact
            <a href="mailto:hello@kadanco.com">hello@kadanco.com</a>.
          </p>

          <h3>Right to lodge a complaint</h3>
          <p>
            You have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority, in particular in the EU
            member state of your residence, place of work or the place of the alleged infringement. The
            authority responsible for us is the Berliner Beauftragte f&uuml;r Datenschutz und
            Informationsfreiheit.
          </p>

          <h3>Storage duration</h3>
          <p>
            We store personal data only for as long as necessary for the stated purpose or as required by
            statutory retention periods, after which it is routinely deleted.
          </p>

          <p style="margin-top:32px"><a href="/">&larr; Back to homepage</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
